From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 16:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: Set FBINFO_VIRTFB on the fbdev framebuffer

msm_fbdev_driver_fbdev_probe() vmaps the buffer object into
fbi->screen_buffer, and msm_fb_ops is built from
FB_GEN_DEFAULT_DEFERRED_SYSMEM_OPS, so every draw goes through the sys_*
helpers. Those helpers warn when FBINFO_VIRTFB is not set:

  fb0: sys_fillrect: framebuffer is not in virtual address space.
  fb0: sys_imageblit: framebuffer is not in virtual address space.

The framebuffer is in virtual address space; the flag was simply never set.
Every other driver in this shape sets it -- drm_fbdev_dma, drm_fbdev_shmem,
omapdrm, exynos and tegra all do.

Signed-off-by: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
@@ -144,6 +144,11 @@
 	fbi->fix.smem_start = paddr;
 	fbi->fix.smem_len = bo->size;
 
+	/* Vmapped system memory, drawn with the sys_* helpers, which warn once
+	 * per operation without this.
+	 */
+	fbi->flags |= FBINFO_VIRTFB;
+
 	DBG("par=%p, %dx%d", fbi->par, fbi->var.xres, fbi->var.yres);
 	DBG("allocated %dx%d fb", fb->width, fb->height);
 
